<title>TURKEY: Turkish 287-d t-bill yield rises to 103.44 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish 287-d t-bill yield rises to 103.44 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield in the Turkish Treasury's 287-day bill auction rose to 103.44 on Friday from 96.47 percent in the previous 287-day bill auction on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Results on page  CBTI.</p>
<p>	Maturity		    : November 26, 1997</p>
<p>	Amount			: 125.6 trln lira</p>
<p>	Coupon			: -</p>
<p>	Minimum yield	     : -</p>
<p>	Maximum yield	     : 103.44</p>
<p>	Average yield	     : -</p>
<p>	Bid amount/cover	  : 205.9 trln</p>
<p>	Lowest accepted price   : 57,123 lira</p>
<p>Pct allocated at lowest price : -</p>
<p>	Payment date		: February 12, 1997</p>
<p>Turkish markets will be closed next Monday and Tuesday for a Moslem holiday and reopen on Wednesday, February 12.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
</text>
